From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:49:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: add g16_resident_lazy to build
 compact render units on demand

With the default g16_resident=8 every render VM builds all eight of its
render units at its first render: two full units and six compact ones,
about 931 MiB per VM, held for as long as the VM lives even when the
client never queues more than one or two renders.

g16_resident_lazy=1 builds only the two full units at the first render.
Each further unit is built in SUBMIT, one at a time and in index order,
when the VM has more render commands outstanding than units built, up to
the resident depth in effect, and is then kept for the life of the VM
like the others. An idle or shallow
client stays near 625 MiB per VM; a deep client grows to the full set.
A failed build leaves the units already built in use.

The units built later live in a per-unit slot next to the first ones and
are reached through accessors (pass, unit_count, units, pool_prepare,
pool_publish, pool_retired, heap_gva, heap_blocks), so the submit, poll
and slot paths do not depend on how many units a VM built at its first
render. The lazy_units stats line reports the builds, their total time in
SUBMIT and the longest one, which is the first-use stall.

The default of 0 keeps the current behaviour: all units at the first
render.

Assisted-by: LLM
